<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Austrian Netherlands</h1><p class="st-meta">1714 CE – 1797 CE · capital Brussels</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The southern Low Countries under Austrian Habsburg rule, a prosperous but contested land whose resistance to Joseph II's reforms foreshadowed Belgium.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaties of Utrecht</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rastatt">Rastatt</a> in 1713–1714 transferred the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-netherlands">Spanish Netherlands</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vi-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Charles VI</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barrier-treaty-1715">Barrier Treaty</a> of 1715 allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> garrisons in a line of fortresses against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governors ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, the most popular being <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-duke-of-lower-lorraine">Charles of Lorraine</a> (1744–1780). The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostend-company">Ostend Company</a>, founded in 1722 to trade with Asia, was suppressed in 1731 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and British pressure. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> occupied the country after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fontenoy">Fontenoy</a> in 1745–1748. Agriculture, roads and industry developed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a>, and Brussels gained neoclassical squares.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Joseph II</a>'s centralising and church reforms sparked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brabant-revolution">Brabant Revolution</a> of 1789 and the short-lived <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-belgian-states">United Belgian States</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> restored control in 1790, but French victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fleurus-1794">Fleurus</a> in 1794 led to annexation in 1795, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-campo-formio">Treaty of Campo Formio</a> in 1797.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/austrian-netherlands.jpg" alt="Austrian Netherlands" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: self made from a low resolution raster version probably by Auseklis or Stijn_Calle, with some elements by Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Austrian_Low_Countries_Flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1714 CE – 1797 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brussels</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles VI, Maria Theresa, Joseph II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch and French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a href="/countries/luxembourg">Luxembourg</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Southern Netherlands (Austrian)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1756&amp;focus=austrian-netherlands" aria-label="Austrian Netherlands on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4779 414 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Austrian Netherlands lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5099 670L5073 659M5099 670L5090 681M5099 670L5098 671M5099 670L5111 681M5099 670L5141 706M5099 670L5102 664M5099 670L5099 670M5099 670L5229 694M5099 670L5381 747M5099 670L5054 728M5099 670L5099 670"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5073 659h0M5090 681h0M5098 671h0M5111 681h0M5141 706h0M5102 664h0M5099 670h0M5229 694h0M5381 747h0M5054